    "result_text": "The change is complete and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` derived field on the owner read model per the spec: it returns `true` when **any** of three soft signals hold, otherwise `false`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `riskFlag` boolean to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is generated from this spec at build time, producing `OwnerDto.setRiskFlag(...)`), documenting the three trigger conditions.\n\n2. **`DisposableEmailDomains.java`** \u2014 Added `isDisposableAdjacent(email)` alongside the existing exact-match `isDisposable(...)`. \"Disposable-adjacent\" means a domain that is *not* itself blocklisted (an exact disposable domain is the stronger signal, already rejected at create time) but is a subdomain of a blocklisted domain (`inbox.mailinator.com`) or shares a blocklisted domain's second-level label under a different suffix (`mailinator.net`). Refactored domain extraction into a shared `domainOf(...)` helper so both checks read the domain identically.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added a `riskFlag(Owner)` helper and wired it into `toOwnerDtoWithDerivedFields(...)`, so both the create and single-owner read paths decorate the owner identically. It aggregates the existing signals:\n   - possible duplicate \u2192 `possibleDuplicateOf != null`\n   - disposable-adjacent email \u2192 `disposableEmailDomains.isDisposableAdjacent(owner.getEmail())`\n   - city over soft capacity \u2192 the existing `capacityWarning(owner.getCity())` band (40\u201349 owners)\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`. The acceptance test `coreRiskFlagFalseNormally` (a fully-unique structured owner with no email \u2192 all three signals false \u2192 `riskFlag` false) passes.",
